---
// The cetra.sh landing page: the holding page made for the PyPI organisation
// review, unchanged except for the documentation link. The marketing site
// replaces it later (D-W-1).
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>cetra</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="cetra is an open-source LLM observability and evaluation platform that runs as one binary on one machine."
    />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://cetra.sh/" />
    <style is:global>
      :root { --bg: #fafaf9; --fg: #1c1917; --muted: #57534e; --link: #0f766e; }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root { --bg: #141414; --fg: #e7e5e4; --muted: #a8a29e; --link: #5eead4; }
      }
      body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg);
        font: 17px/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; }
      main { max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 72px 16px; }
      h1 { font-size: 2.2rem; margin: 0 0 8px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
      .tag { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 32px; }
      a { color: var(--link); }
      ul { padding-left: 20px; }
      footer { margin-top: 48px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>cetra</h1>
      <p class="tag">Open-source LLM observability and evaluation.</p>

      <p>cetra records the traces of LLM applications, measures their cost and latency, and evaluates their output. It runs as one binary on one machine: OpenTelemetry ingestion, its own storage engine, and a web UI, with Python and TypeScript SDKs.</p>

      <p>cetra is in development and has not been released yet.</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Documentation: <a href="/docs/">cetra.sh/docs</a></li>
        <li>Source code: <a href="https://github.com/cetra-ai/cetra">github.com/cetra-ai/cetra</a></li>
        <li>Licence: MIT, with a few enterprise directories under the Elastic License 2.0 (<a href="https://github.com/cetra-ai/cetra/blob/main/LICENSE">details</a>)</li>
        <li>Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@cetra.sh">hello@cetra.sh</a></li>
      </ul>

      <footer>cetra.sh</footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
